orm L101:     * AVAILABLE ADD-ONS\nL102:       * cite11†GitHub Advanced SecurityEnterprise-grade security features L103:       * cite58†Copilot for BusinessEnterprise-grade AI features L104:       * cite59†Premium SupportEnterprise-grade 24/7 support L105: \nL106:   * cite60†Pricing L107: \nL108: Search`/`\nL109: \nL110: cite1†Sign in L111: \nL112: cite61†Sign up L113: \nL114: Appearance settings\nL115: You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. Dismiss alert\nL116: \nL117: cite62†Image: @MoonshotAI†avatars.githubusercontent.com L118: # Moonshot AI\nL119: \nL120:   *   * cite63†9.8k followers L121:   * cite64†https://moonshot.ai†moonshot.ai L122: \nL123:   * cite2†Overview L124:   * cite65†Repositories L125:   * cite66†Projects L126:   * cite67†Packages L127:   * cite68†People L128: \nL129: More\nL130: \nL131: cite69†README.md L132: \nL133: # Welcome to Moonshot AI\nL134: \nL135: cite64†Moonshot AI†moonshot.ai is committed to solving ambitious \"moonshot\" problems that will lead humanity to AGI. We embrace open source, and contributed the following projects to the community:\nL136: ## Research\nL137:   * cite70†Kimi K3 : Kimi K3 is a 2.8T-parameter model built on Kimi Delta Attention (KDA) and Attention Residuals (AttnRes), with native vision capabilities and a 1-million-token context window. It is the world's first open 3T-class model, designed for frontier intelligence across long-horizon coding, knowledge work, and reasoning.\nL138:   * cite71†Attention Residuals : a drop-in replacement for residual connections with consistent scaling gains.\nL139:   * cite72†Kimi K2.5 : Kimi K2.5 is an open-source, native multimodal agentic model built through continual pretraining on approximately 15 trillion mixed visual and text tokens atop Kimi-K2-Base.\nL140:   * cite73†Kimi Linear : a hybrid linear attention architecture that outperforms traditional full attention methods across various contexts.\nL141:   * cite74†Kimi K2 : an open-source Mixture-of-Experts model with 32B activated parameters and 1T total parameters. It achieves state-of-the-art performance in frontier knowledge, math, and coding among non-thinking models.\nL142:   * cite75†Kimi-K1.5 : Scaling Reinforcement Learning with LLMs. We released our tech report on building an o1-level multi-modal reasoning model.\nL143:   * cite76†Moonlight for our paper cite77†Muon is Scalable for LLM Training†arxiv.org . We released (i) checkpoints for SOTA small models; (ii) code for our improved Muon optimizer.\nL144:   * cite78†MoBA : Mixture of Block Attention for Long-Context LLMs. We released code and paper for our looong-context LLM technique.\nL145:   * cite79†Kimi-VL : Mixture-of-Experts Vision-Language Model for Multimodal Reasoning, Long-Context Understanding, and Strong Agent Capabilities\nL146:   * cite80†Kimina-Prover Preview : Towards Large Formal Reasoning Models with Reinforcement Learning. We released technical report, model weights and a rectified version of miniF2F-test benchmark.\nL147:   * cite81†Kimi-Audio : Universal audio foundation model that handles diverse tasks like speech recognition, audio understanding, audio-to-text chat, speech-to-speech conversation. We released the technical report, model weights and evaluation toolkit.\nL148: ## Benchmarks\nL149: \nL150:   * cite82†WorldVQA : a benchmark measuring atomic vision-centric world knowledge in multimodal large language models.\nL151:   * cite83†PerceptionBench : a benchmark for evaluating atomic visual perception in multimodal large language models.\nL152:   * cite84†CombiBench : the first benchmark for combinatorial mathematics problems formalized in Lean 4.\nL153: \nL154: ## Agents\nL155: \nL156:   * cite85†Kimi Code : A fast, versatile, and extensible AI coding agent that brings Kimi into your projects and development workflow.\nL157: ## Service and Infra\nL158:   * cite86†MoonEP : an expert parallelism communication library that keeps token loads perfectly balanced across ranks via dynamic redundant experts.\nL159:   * cite87†FlashKDA : high-performance Kimi Delta Attention kernels built on CUTLASS.\nL160:   * cite88†Kimi-Vendor-Verifier : monitoring and verifying the precision of Kimi model APIs across vendors.\nL161:   * cite89†checkpoint-engine : efficiently update model weights in LLM serving.\nL162:   * cite90†Mooncake : pioneered the idea of KV-centric disaggregated LLM serving, winning the Best Paper award at FAST 2025. We released code and data corresponding to our paper.\nL163:   * cite91†moonpalace : debugging tool for our API service.\nL164: ## Community\nL165: \nL166:   * cite92†Forum†forum.moonshot.ai : join discussions, ask questions, and share ideas about the Moonshot AI platform and APIs.\nL167: ## Pinned Loading\nL168: \nL169:   1. cite85†kimi-code kimi-code Public\nL170: \nL171: Kimi Code CLI — The Starting Point for Next-Gen Agents\nL172: \nL173: TypeScript cite93†7.8k cite94†1.3k L174: \nL175:   2. cite71†Attention-Residuals Attention-Residuals Public\nL176: \nL177: cite95†3.5k cite96†204 L178: \nL179:   3. cite70†Kimi-K3 Kimi-K3 Public\nL180: \nL181: Open Frontier Intelligence\nL182: \nL183: cite97†8.9k cite98†751 L184: \nL185:   4. cite87†FlashKDA FlashKDA Public\nL186: \nL187: FlashKDA: high-performance Kimi Delta Attention kernels\nL188: \nL189: Cuda cite99†1.3k cite100†122 L190: \nL191:   5. cite86†MoonEP MoonEP Public\nL192: MoonEP: A Perfectly Balanced Expert Parallelism Library via Dynamic Redundant Experts\nL193: \nL194: Python cite101†1.2k cite102†134 L195: \nL196:   6. cite103†K2-Vendor-Verifier K2-Vendor-Verifier Public\nL197: \nL198: Verify Precision of all Kimi K2 API Vendor\nL199: \nL20